response.value:
The easiest option is to use **CSS `filter`**, but it will affect the entire canvas—not only the snake:

```css
canvas {
  transition: filter 1s ease;
}
```

For a transition affecting **only the snake**, canvas has no built-in transition. You need to gradually change the RGB values in your game loop.

A simpler visual alternative is to add intermediate score levels:

```js
if (score >= 5) ctx.fillStyle = "lightgreen";
if (score >= 8) ctx.fillStyle = "yellow";
if (score >= 10) ctx.fillStyle = "orange";
```

This is easier, but it changes color instantly rather than smoothly.

